1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,147
Most footballers retire around thirty-five.

2
00:00:02,347 --> 00:00:05,035
Players his age are on TV, talking about football.

3
00:00:05,235 --> 00:00:09,416
Cristiano Ronaldo is forty-one. And he's still chasing one thousand goals.

4
00:00:09,616 --> 00:00:10,832
How? Let's follow his day.

5
00:00:11,232 --> 00:00:14,197
Morning. He wakes up rested, because he treats sleep like training.

6
00:00:14,397 --> 00:00:17,021
Reportedly, that even includes short naps through the day.

7
00:00:17,221 --> 00:00:19,483
Breakfast? Lots of protein. Very little sugar.

8
00:00:19,683 --> 00:00:23,331
He once moved two soda bottles off a press table and held up water.

9
00:00:23,531 --> 00:00:25,344
And alcohol? He's said he doesn't drink.

10
00:00:25,744 --> 00:00:29,157
Then training. Sprints. Weights. Extra shooting after everyone leaves.

11
00:00:29,357 --> 00:00:31,341
Teammates often say: first in, last out.

12
00:00:31,541 --> 00:00:33,952
That's how a forty-one year old still jumps like this.

13
00:00:34,152 --> 00:00:36,947
One header was measured at over two and a half meters high.

14
00:00:37,147 --> 00:00:39,557
After? Ice cold recovery. Brrr.

15
00:00:39,757 --> 00:00:41,784
Then rest. Then repeat. Every single day.

16
00:00:42,184 --> 00:00:44,445
The result? Over nine hundred and seventy goals.

17
00:00:44,645 --> 00:00:47,120
More goals for his country than any man in history.

18
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:49,581
Six World Cups. A league title at forty-one.

19
00:00:49,781 --> 00:00:52,149
Talent got him started. Habits kept him going.

20
00:00:52,349 --> 00:00:56,104
So next time you skip a workout, remember who's still training at forty-one.

